teh4k3000-by-theolddude for Debian
----------------------------------

The upstream archive (entry_teh4k.zip on scene.org) contains no source
code, only two executables:
 - teh4k.run, the packed 4k version. It unpacks itself to /tmp/I and runs
   it from there, so it is not installed;
 - teh4k, a bigger executable built with debug information. This is the
   one installed in /usr/lib/i386-linux-gnu/teh4k3000-by-theolddude.

The executable starts fullscreen in 1280x720, or in a window when it gets
the -w option: the launcher uses -w. It already asks for V-Sync
(SDL_GL_SWAP_CONTROL before SDL_SetVideoMode). Any key quits; closing the
window does nothing, as the intro only checks SDL_KEYDOWN events.

The launcher uses sdl12-compat (SDL 1.2 API on top of SDL 2) through
LD_LIBRARY_PATH, with the X11 video driver. The executable cannot be
hardened: the lintian tags about hardening are overridden.

executable seems to be compiled for Fedora 13

GCC: (GNU) 4.4.4 20100630 (Red Hat 4.4.4-10)

Source files:
-------------
crtstuff.c esimsong.c main.c syntinen.c teh4k_gfx.c

